he first non-stop transatlantic flight from Paris to New York City. It was piloted by French World War I aviation heroes Charles Nungesser and his navigator Francois Coli as part of the competition for the $25,000 Orteig Prize. The aircraft's attempt ended in mystery, as it was last seen over Ireland, while Charles Lindbergh later successfully completed the journey in the 'Spirit of St. Louis.'?", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}], "final_answer": "Charles Nungesser", "total_time": 35.643535137176514, "retrieval_rounds": 2}, "question_id": "5ae0361155429925eb1afc2c", "prompt_tokens": 8617, "completion_tokens": 1341, "total_tokens": 9958, "llm_call_count": 3, "total_llm_latency_seconds": 35.4718, "mean_llm_call_latency_seconds": 11.8239}
