, he reassumed the Spanish throne when Louis died, continuing his reign until his own death in 1746.", "analysis": "The documents explicitly mention Philip V's reign, abdication in favor of his son Louis, and his subsequent resumption of the throne following his son's death. This directly answers the sub-question about the reason for his resumption of the throne."}}, "reasoning_process": "Analyzing documents for: Why did Philip V resume the throne?", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}], "final_answer": "Philip V resumed the throne upon the death of his son Louis in 1724. After initially abdicating in favor of his son in 1724, he reassumed the Spanish throne when Louis died, continuing his reign until his own death in 1746.", "total_time": 37.74503946304321, "retrieval_rounds": 2}, "question_id": "5add016e5542992c1e3a250b", "prompt_tokens": 12337, "completion_tokens": 1391, "total_tokens": 13728, "llm_call_count": 3, "total_llm_latency_seconds": 37.6153, "mean_llm_call_latency_seconds": 12.5384}
