 U.S. 57, 1981), stating the Court upheld the constitutionality of requiring only men to register for the draft. These documents directly address the sub-question's legal ruling and the specific practice in question."}}, "reasoning_process": "Analyzing documents for: What practice of filling armed forces vacancies was deemed constitutional by In Rostker v. Goldberg (453 U.S. 57, 1981), the United States Supreme Court ruled that the practice of requiring only men to register for the draft was constitutional. The Court held that the gender distinction did not violate the Equal Protection Clause of the Due Process Clause, upholding the law as passed by Congress.?", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}], "final_answer": "The practice deemed constitutional by the Supreme Court in Rostker v. Goldberg (1981) was requiring only men to register for the draft. The Court ruled this gender distinction did not violate the Equal Protection Clause of the Due Process Clause, upholding Congress's law as passed.", "total_time": 29.429879188537598, "retrieval_rounds": 2}, "question_id": "5a88658955429938390d3f47", "prompt_tokens": 11961, "completion_tokens": 1061, "total_tokens": 13022, "llm_call_count": 3, "total_llm_latency_seconds": 29.27, "mean_llm_call_latency_seconds": 9.7567}
